ff the cruise control either by depressing the brake pedal or manually turning the system off once it has been engaged, resulting in either the vehicle maintaining its current speed or possibly accelerating.","consequence":"If the vehicle maintains its speed or accelerates despite attempts to deactivate the cruise control, there would be an increased risk of a crash.","remedy":"Chrysler will notify owners, and dealers will inspect the software, and perform a software flash on the engine or powertrain control module, free of charge.  The recall began June 4, 2018.  Owners may contact Chrysler customer service at 1-800-853-1403.  Note: Owners are advised to stop using cruise control until the software update has been performed.  In the event that cruise control cannot be disengaged while driving, owners should firmly and steadily apply the brakes and shift the transmission to neutral, placing the vehicle in park once it has stopped.","park_it":false,"park_outside":false,"over_the_air":false,"has_potential_units":true,"potential_units":4815661,"potential_units_source_url":"https://api.nhtsa.gov/recalls/campaignNumber?campaignNumber=18V332000","potential_units_source_title":"NHTSA Recalls API (campaignNumber)","campaign_vehicle_count":66,"campaign_vehicles":[{"year":"2014","make":"JEEP","model":"GRAND CHEROKEE"},{"year":"2014","make":"RAM","model":"2500"},{"year":"2014","make":"JEEP","model":"CHEROKEE"},{"year":"2014","make":"DODGE","model":"CHARGER"},{"year":"2014","make":"CHRYSLER","model":"300"},{"year":"2014","make":"DODGE","model":"DURANGO"},{"year":"2014","make":"RAM","model":"5500"},{"year":"2014","make":"DODGE","model":"JOURNEY"},{"year":"2014","make":"RAM","model":"1500"},{"year":"2015","make":"RAM","model":"5500"},{"year":"2015","make":"CHRYSLER","model":"300"},{"year":"2015","make":"DODGE","model":"CHARGER"},{"year":"2015","make":"DODGE","model":"DURANGO"},{"year":"2015","make":"RAM","model":"1500"},{"year":"2014","make":"RAM","model":"3500"},{"year":"2014","